`buildShareUrl` interpolates `objectName`, `viewId`, and `token` directly into the URL path/query. If any contain characters like `/`, `?`, `#`, or spaces, the generated URL will be malformed. Use `encodeURIComponent` (and ideally `new URL()` for query params) when constructing the share URL components.
```suggestion
  const url = new URL(
    `${baseUrl.replace(/\/+$/, '')}/share/${encodeURIComponent(objectName)}/${encodeURIComponent(viewId)}`
  );
  url.searchParams.set('mode', 'readonly');
  url.searchParams.set('token', token);
  return url.toString();
```

`undo()`/`redo()` remove the operation from the manager (`popUndo`/`popRedo`) before verifying that an execution can succeed. If `dataSource` is missing (or the data operation throws), history is still mutated (op moved stacks) and the operation is effectively lost / ends up on the wrong stack. Consider peeking first, executing, and only moving the op between stacks after a successful dataSource call; also avoid changing history at all when `dataSource` is undefined.
```suggestion
    if (!ds) {
      throw new Error('No dataSource provided for undo/redo operation.');
    }
    const action = mode === 'undo'
      ? ({ create: 'delete', update: 'update', delete: 'create' } as const)[op.type]
      : op.type;
    if (action === 'delete') {
      await ds.delete(op.objectName, op.recordId);
    } else if (action === 'update') {
      await ds.update(op.objectName, op.recordId, data);
    } else {
      await ds.create(op.objectName, data);
    }
  }, []);

  const undo = useCallback(async () => {
    const op = globalUndoManager.peekUndo();
    if (!op) return;
    try {
      await executeOp(op, op.undoData, 'undo');
    } catch {
      // Do not mutate history if execution fails (including missing dataSource).
      return;
    }
    globalUndoManager.popUndo();
    optionsRef.current.onUndo?.(op);
  }, [executeOp]);

  const redo = useCallback(async () => {
    const op = globalUndoManager.peekRedo();
    if (!op) return;
    try {
      await executeOp(op, op.redoData, 'redo');
    } catch {
      // Do not mutate history if execution fails (including missing dataSource).
      return;
    }
    globalUndoManager.popRedo();
```

`dataSource` is typed as `any`, which bypasses the repo’s `DataSource` abstraction and makes it easy to call non-existent methods. Consider typing this as `DataSource` (from `@object-ui/types`) or a narrow subset of it (e.g., `{ create: DataSource['create']; bulk?: DataSource['bulk'] }`) so the import flow stays backend-agnostic and type-safe.
```suggestion
import type { DataSource } from '@object-ui/types';
import { Upload, FileSpreadsheet, CheckCircle2, AlertCircle, X, ArrowRight, ArrowLeft } from 'lucide-react';

export interface ImportWizardProps {
  objectName: string;
  objectLabel?: string;
  fields: Array<{ name: string; label: string; type: string; required?: boolean }>;
  dataSource: DataSource;
```
